WEBVTT

00:06.600 --> 00:07.625
[theme song playing]

00:07.725 --> 00:09.885
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.136 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.395
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.479 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:26.652
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:30.781
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.823 --> 00:35.619
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.702 --> 00:39.498
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.581 --> 00:43.460
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.544 --> 00:44.545
[song concludes]

00:44.628 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:46.838 --> 00:48.882
[in Korean]
If writing a petition is too much trouble,

00:48.966 --> 00:50.717
you can just sign the form and…

00:52.302 --> 00:54.972
No, I'm not trying to force you.

00:55.681 --> 00:58.100
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:58.183 --> 01:00.269
- Thank you for your…
- [cell phone beeps]

01:01.645 --> 01:02.646
[groans]

01:04.106 --> 01:06.733
- [quirky music playing]
- [sighs] I got rejected again.

01:06.817 --> 01:09.820
Why is it that the more I try,
the worse I do?

01:09.903 --> 01:12.406
Is it obvious that I've never worked
in the real world?

01:12.489 --> 01:14.992
I can't even persuade people
over the phone…

01:15.075 --> 01:17.244
Stop. Of course you can persuade people.

01:17.744 --> 01:19.705
You even managed to convince Ms. Sang-wol.

01:19.788 --> 01:23.709
That's already in the past.
Maybe I've lost my touch now.

01:23.792 --> 01:26.044
Mi-ji, that's not something
that just anyone can do.

01:27.254 --> 01:30.048
Everything you've accomplished
is still a part of you.

01:30.132 --> 01:33.010
This was just a simple rejection.

01:33.719 --> 01:34.886
Don't doubt yourself.

01:37.681 --> 01:39.349
Yes, wise one.

01:39.433 --> 01:42.894
- [laughs] Jeez…
- [Mi-ji chuckles]

01:42.978 --> 01:44.104
[computer chimes]

01:44.187 --> 01:45.397
I got an email.

01:45.480 --> 01:47.357
[music fades]

01:49.151 --> 01:50.402
[Ho-su] Is there…

01:51.320 --> 01:53.822
anything you want to do
after all this is over?

01:53.905 --> 01:55.866
What? That's a random question.

01:55.949 --> 01:58.952
We didn't even get to celebrate
your birthday properly.

01:59.036 --> 02:02.331
Should we go somewhere?
Or is there something you want?

02:05.876 --> 02:09.254
If I had to pick something…

02:09.338 --> 02:12.799
It does feel a bit empty here.

02:12.883 --> 02:15.093
Is it your bangs?

02:15.719 --> 02:16.970
Jeez.

02:17.054 --> 02:18.597
Forget it.

02:19.306 --> 02:20.349
[chuckles softly]

02:20.432 --> 02:21.933
[gentle music playing]

02:22.017 --> 02:24.811
[Ho-su] A today that's a little better
than yesterday.

02:24.895 --> 02:25.979
[sighs]

02:29.524 --> 02:33.362
Those todays
build the promise of a tomorrow.

02:36.156 --> 02:38.241
The promise to be together tomorrow too…

02:39.326 --> 02:41.953
I'm here to buy rings
for my girlfriend and me.

02:42.037 --> 02:43.538
This is her ring size.

02:44.039 --> 02:46.124
…when things will be
even better than today.

02:46.208 --> 02:48.085
- [door chime clinking]
- [gentle music continues]

02:48.168 --> 02:49.795
[cell phone buzzing]

02:50.462 --> 02:51.755
RING

02:53.215 --> 02:54.257
Hello.

02:55.092 --> 02:56.426
It is arrogant…

02:58.011 --> 02:59.054
Hello?

03:00.681 --> 03:02.432
…to promise a tomorrow together…

03:02.516 --> 03:04.017
- [music fades]
- [sound fades]

03:04.101 --> 03:05.644
…when I don't even know…

03:06.853 --> 03:08.188
what will happen to me today.

03:08.271 --> 03:09.356
[muffled] Hello?

03:13.151 --> 03:14.653
[silence]

03:14.736 --> 03:18.907
EPISODE 11
AT THE END OF THE SENTENCE

03:18.990 --> 03:20.158
ROSA RESTAURANT
SELF-LIT SIGN

03:20.242 --> 03:21.368
ROSE
ACRYLIC BOX? NEON SIGN?

03:21.451 --> 03:25.163
I didn't realize you meant
you would draw these by hand.

03:25.247 --> 03:26.604
No.

03:26.707 --> 03:30.585
I just wanted to give you a general idea
before we send it to the sign shop.

03:30.669 --> 03:32.087
Which one is your favorite?

03:33.672 --> 03:35.090
Let me think about it.

03:35.924 --> 03:36.925
Okay.

03:37.626 --> 03:40.212
By the way, why are you here alone?
Where's Ho-su?

03:40.320 --> 03:43.180
Someone he knew passed away. Remember?

03:43.280 --> 03:44.891
He'll be back tomorrow after the funeral.

03:44.975 --> 03:48.270
He's coming back tomorrow?
He's been gone for a while.

03:49.245 --> 03:51.038
Was he very close to them?

03:51.106 --> 03:53.191
I didn't get the chance
to ask him about it.

03:53.275 --> 03:55.444
He seemed too distracted
to even talk on the phone.

03:55.527 --> 03:56.528
Gosh…

03:57.154 --> 03:59.030
I was going to give him
some marinated raw crabs.

03:59.114 --> 04:00.991
What? Marinated raw crabs?

04:01.074 --> 04:02.325
What about me?

04:02.409 --> 04:03.994
I gave you your share yesterday.

04:04.077 --> 04:05.787
But I've almost finished it.

04:06.705 --> 04:09.374
Come on! I even drew
some sign designs for you.

04:09.458 --> 04:13.420
I figured that Ho-su would end up
sharing them with you anyway,

04:13.503 --> 04:15.714
so I made enough for two people.

04:17.132 --> 04:18.216
[in English] Yes!

04:21.094 --> 04:24.055
[in Korean] This is heavy, though.
Should I wait until Ho-su comes back?

04:24.139 --> 04:25.640
No, I can take it.

04:25.724 --> 04:28.185
I'll drop it off at his place
on my way home.

04:28.852 --> 04:30.604
Make sure you put it in the fridge.

04:30.687 --> 04:32.147
Don't eat it all by yourself.

04:33.523 --> 04:34.524
Yes, ma'am.

04:34.608 --> 04:36.067
[Mi-ji chuckles softly]

04:40.405 --> 04:44.075
- [automated voice] The person you're…
- Why isn't he picking up?

04:45.202 --> 04:46.453
[door lock beeping]

04:47.454 --> 04:48.538
[door lock beeps rapidly]

04:48.622 --> 04:49.790
What?

04:52.834 --> 04:53.794
[door lock beeps rapidly]

04:53.877 --> 04:54.878
Oh…

04:57.005 --> 04:58.173
[door lock chimes]

04:59.424 --> 05:00.884
[gasps] Ho-su.

05:01.384 --> 05:04.888
When did you get back?
You said you were coming back tomorrow.

05:04.971 --> 05:07.557
Things wrapped up earlier than planned.

05:07.641 --> 05:11.019
Hey! You should've called me then!

05:11.102 --> 05:13.271
I called you and you didn't even pick up.

05:13.772 --> 05:15.524
Also, did you change your passcode?

05:18.109 --> 05:19.486
What is it?

05:20.028 --> 05:22.656
Is someone inside?

05:23.490 --> 05:24.866
No, nobody's inside.

05:25.700 --> 05:27.035
It's just that today is…

05:28.745 --> 05:30.038
You're sick again, aren't you?

05:31.039 --> 05:32.249
No, it's not that.

05:32.332 --> 05:34.000
Don't lie to me.

05:34.084 --> 05:36.127
Your face is telling me a different story.

05:36.211 --> 05:39.172
Who passed away?
It seems like you've worn yourself out.

05:39.840 --> 05:41.383
Did you take any medication?

05:41.883 --> 05:43.635
Let me see if you have a fever.

05:45.345 --> 05:46.930
I'm just a bit tired.

05:47.514 --> 05:48.807
Let's meet up tomorrow.

05:49.307 --> 05:50.225
Okay.

05:50.767 --> 05:52.644
All right, then…

05:53.770 --> 05:54.855
But this…

05:54.938 --> 05:56.857
[door lock clanks, chimes]

05:56.940 --> 05:58.525
What in the world?

06:01.152 --> 06:02.153
[kicking on ground]

06:02.237 --> 06:04.573
Fine. I'm just going to eat this
all by myself.

06:07.951 --> 06:09.202
[high-pitched ringing]

06:09.286 --> 06:10.412
[Ho-su groans]

06:11.037 --> 06:13.456
- [pensive music playing]
- [Ho-su sobs softly]

06:13.540 --> 06:15.959
[ringing continues]

06:17.419 --> 06:19.838
- [door chime clinking]
- [pensive music continues]

06:20.422 --> 06:21.339
I…

06:22.090 --> 06:23.466
need to take this call real quick.

06:23.550 --> 06:24.926
Okay.

06:35.103 --> 06:37.564
Sir, please take me to HNU Hospital.

06:38.315 --> 06:40.150
[driver] This taxi is Incheon-bound.

06:42.611 --> 06:44.905
HNU Hospital, please.

06:45.614 --> 06:48.950
[driver] I just told you that
this taxi is heading to Incheon.

06:49.034 --> 06:51.119
[muffled]
I'm not headed in that direction.

06:51.202 --> 06:52.287
Please just get out.

06:52.370 --> 06:54.706
[pensive music continues]

06:54.789 --> 06:56.750
[driver speaking inaudibly]

07:00.295 --> 07:02.547
[pensive music continues]

07:08.803 --> 07:09.846
[doctor] Heart.

07:11.139 --> 07:12.349
[over headphones] Human.

07:13.850 --> 07:14.893
Ocean.

07:14.976 --> 07:17.187
INTRATYMPANIC STEROID INJECTION
HIGH-DOSE TREATMENT

07:18.813 --> 07:20.315
[nurse] Mr. Lee Ho-su.

07:20.899 --> 07:22.984
EAR, NOSE, AND THROAT

07:23.068 --> 07:24.986
Is there a Mr. Lee Ho-su here?

07:27.614 --> 07:29.824
- Are you Mr. Lee Ho-su?
- Yes.

07:30.867 --> 07:33.328
[doctor] You have
sudden sensorineural hearing loss.

07:33.411 --> 07:37.582
For now, let's try injecting steroids
into the eardrum for the next few days.

07:37.666 --> 07:39.542
If there's any improvement,
we can reassess.

07:39.626 --> 07:40.627
[pensive music continues]

07:40.710 --> 07:44.381
For sudden hearing loss, the prognosis
generally falls into three categories.

07:44.464 --> 07:47.425
Your hearing might get better,
stay as it is, or be lost for good.

07:48.510 --> 07:50.637
But as you can see here,

07:51.221 --> 07:52.973
you're not doing too great.

07:54.099 --> 07:55.600
Given the higher dose of the injection,

07:55.684 --> 07:57.978
I was hoping at least 80%
of your hearing would've returned.

07:58.061 --> 07:59.104
Then…

07:59.688 --> 08:01.439
of the three possible outcomes…

08:01.523 --> 08:03.942
It's hard to tell
if your hearing will remain the same

08:04.025 --> 08:05.735
or get worse at this point.

08:06.277 --> 08:08.196
There's a chance
it could improve miraculously,

08:08.279 --> 08:11.366
but your hearing is down
across all frequencies.

08:11.908 --> 08:13.910
So a full recovery is unlikely.

08:16.705 --> 08:17.706
Then…

08:20.667 --> 08:23.128
what should I do now?

08:23.211 --> 08:24.754
[doctor sighing] Well,

08:25.380 --> 08:27.841
you've regained at least some hearing,

08:27.924 --> 08:31.594
so let's continue the outpatient visits
and monitor your progress for now.

08:31.678 --> 08:33.596
You're telling me to do nothing

08:33.680 --> 08:37.017
when we don't know the cause
or whether it'll get better or worse?

08:37.100 --> 08:40.145
What if I completely lose hearing
in this ear as well?

08:40.770 --> 08:44.482
Well, hearing aids or a cochlear implant
could be considered,

08:44.983 --> 08:46.985
but that's only if things get a lot worse.

08:48.236 --> 08:49.946
You mean there's nothing I can do…

08:52.073 --> 08:53.700
until things get worse?

08:55.160 --> 08:56.224
HIGH-DOSE STEROID INJECTION

08:56.336 --> 08:58.967
[doctor] What's more important
than medications or injections is…

08:59.622 --> 09:01.416
remaining calm and mentally stable.

09:01.499 --> 09:04.836
You need to brace yourself
and prepare for the worst-case scenario.

09:05.920 --> 09:08.548
[door lock beeping]

09:08.631 --> 09:10.175
[music fades]

09:10.258 --> 09:11.968
- [door lock chimes]
- [gasps]

09:12.052 --> 09:13.428
Ho-su.

09:13.511 --> 09:16.765
When did you get back?
You said you were coming back tomorrow.

09:16.848 --> 09:19.309
Things wrapped up earlier than planned.

09:19.392 --> 09:22.937
- [high-pitched ringing]
- Hey! You should've called me then!

09:23.021 --> 09:25.774
[muffled] I called you
and you didn't even pick up.

09:26.441 --> 09:28.568
- I'm just a bit tired.
- [ringing fades]

09:28.651 --> 09:29.778
[somber music playing]

09:29.861 --> 09:31.404
Let's meet up tomorrow.

09:31.488 --> 09:32.530
[Mi-ji] But this…

09:32.614 --> 09:34.407
[door lock beeps, chimes]

09:34.491 --> 09:36.743
- [groans]
- [high-pitched ringing]

09:50.882 --> 09:53.176
[groans, breathes shakily]

09:57.430 --> 09:58.556
[music concludes]

09:58.640 --> 10:00.558
Tae-i, do you have
the documents I asked for?

10:00.642 --> 10:02.685
- I really need them now.
- I'm doing them in order.

10:02.769 --> 10:04.020
But…

10:06.314 --> 10:07.482
What in the world?

10:07.565 --> 10:09.609
[dramatic tense music playing]

10:10.693 --> 10:13.738
Where is Mr. Shin Gyeong-min?

10:14.614 --> 10:16.866
Over here. Who are you?

10:17.492 --> 10:19.619
We're from the Fair Trade Commission.

10:19.702 --> 10:23.206
We're investigating the Sihan Construction
case, so please cooperate.

10:23.289 --> 10:24.332
Pardon?

10:26.417 --> 10:27.919
Go this way, and get the computer too.

10:28.002 --> 10:30.168
INVESTIGATING VIOLATIONS
OF ANTITRUST AND FAIR TRADE LAWS

10:30.255 --> 10:32.757
[Gyeong-min] Wait. Don't touch that.
Hold on. That's…

10:33.383 --> 10:35.385
Stop. Hold on.

10:36.177 --> 10:38.638
KFMC'S ALLEGED PREFERENTIAL TREATMENT
OF SIHAN CONSTRUCTION

10:38.721 --> 10:39.973
[cell phone buzzing]

10:40.056 --> 10:41.057
SHIN GYEONG-MIN

10:42.100 --> 10:45.103
You've stirred up all this noise
because you couldn't buy one restaurant.

10:45.186 --> 10:48.022
What are you going to do now?
They've even released an article.

10:48.106 --> 10:51.192
I'll contact the press
and have them correct--

10:51.276 --> 10:53.194
What's the point? The damage is done!

10:53.278 --> 10:57.448
This is why I specifically asked you
to handle this as quietly as possible!

10:57.532 --> 10:59.075
[sighs] I'm sorry, sir.

10:59.868 --> 11:02.120
But it's just one article so far.

11:02.203 --> 11:03.288
If we manage the press--

11:03.371 --> 11:04.622
[CEO] Last time,

11:04.706 --> 11:07.792
you said it was just one anonymous post,
so you'd handle it.

11:07.876 --> 11:11.880
How will you take responsibility for this?
Are you even capable of doing that?

11:12.505 --> 11:13.590
My gosh.

11:16.551 --> 11:17.886
[music concludes]

11:18.511 --> 11:20.013
[cell phone buzzing]

11:20.930 --> 11:23.099
Gosh, why weren't you picking up?

11:23.641 --> 11:25.518
Have you seen the article?
It's on the main page.

11:25.602 --> 11:27.228
I was in a meeting.

11:27.729 --> 11:29.397
Yes, I read it on my way to work.

11:29.480 --> 11:31.608
[Se-jin] Now that the article's out,

11:31.691 --> 11:33.818
there's no way
they can just cover this up now.

11:33.902 --> 11:35.069
Thank you.

11:35.153 --> 11:37.113
For what? I didn't write it.

11:37.614 --> 11:40.909
You introduced me to the reporter
and gave me advice on everything.

11:40.992 --> 11:42.577
I couldn't have done this by myself.

11:42.660 --> 11:44.787
[Se-jin] You were doing just fine
on your own too.

11:44.871 --> 11:46.456
I just sped things up

11:46.539 --> 11:48.499
so my business partner
can come back here sooner.

11:48.583 --> 11:49.626
I didn't do anything.

11:49.709 --> 11:52.170
[Mi-rae] That's not true.
Thank you. I mean it.

11:52.837 --> 11:54.047
Enough of that.

11:54.130 --> 11:57.508
Anyway, what about the FTC?
Shouldn't they start investigating soon?

12:01.012 --> 12:02.096
It looks like they're here.

12:08.102 --> 12:10.355
[Tae-i] The FTC was your doing, right?

12:11.439 --> 12:12.649
Yes.

12:13.149 --> 12:14.567
Why did you go to HR earlier?

12:16.778 --> 12:19.697
Did they summon you
because they know you reported them?

12:19.781 --> 12:20.698
No.

12:21.199 --> 12:23.743
I had a meeting regarding
workplace bullying.

12:23.826 --> 12:26.412
I thought it'd be better
to do it before I quit.

12:26.496 --> 12:27.580
You're leaving?

12:28.456 --> 12:29.707
Why…

12:31.709 --> 12:34.337
[sighs] The hard part
is almost done now, though.

12:34.837 --> 12:38.424
Don't you feel like it'd be a waste
to quit now after everything?

12:38.508 --> 12:41.302
You should stick around
to see them get punished.

12:41.386 --> 12:43.429
I don't really see the point in that.

12:44.806 --> 12:48.559
Honestly, I've just been hanging on
because I didn't want to lose.

12:49.310 --> 12:53.189
I wanted to stand my ground
and prove to them I wasn't at fault.

12:54.190 --> 12:57.151
I'm sure seeing them punished
would bring some relief.

12:57.235 --> 13:00.571
But sticking around just to see that

13:01.155 --> 13:03.324
doesn't feel like
it's in my best interest.

13:04.617 --> 13:08.079
My heart still pounds anxiously
every time I come to work.

13:08.162 --> 13:09.872
[soft pensive music playing]

13:09.956 --> 13:13.042
It's not exactly
a satisfying ending, is it?

13:15.962 --> 13:18.172
But how you feel is what matters the most.

13:19.549 --> 13:21.551
I pushed you into doing this with me,

13:22.176 --> 13:25.555
but I ended up making you do it
all by yourself, just like you said.

13:26.180 --> 13:27.515
That's not true.

13:27.598 --> 13:30.643
I'm going to leave you
with the task I dreaded the most.

13:31.602 --> 13:36.733
I want you to stay here for me
and keep an eye on things.

13:36.816 --> 13:39.193
See how this all ends,

13:39.277 --> 13:42.780
and then tell me everything later.

13:51.873 --> 13:54.250
[Bun-hong]
Ho-su, are you busy these days?

13:54.334 --> 13:57.795
The teachers at our school
must have read the articles about you.

13:57.879 --> 14:01.257
They're asking if you could come
and be a guest lecturer for a day.

14:01.841 --> 14:03.468
[automated voice]
The person you're trying…

14:03.551 --> 14:04.594
[cell phone buzzes]

14:04.677 --> 14:06.576
SON

14:06.763 --> 14:10.224
[Ho-su] I've got a lot of work right now,
so I can't come for a while.

14:11.184 --> 14:12.977
[soft pensive music continues]

14:15.271 --> 14:17.273
[Bun-hong] Of course, work comes first.

14:17.357 --> 14:20.485
No matter how busy you are,
make sure you take care of yourself.

14:21.069 --> 14:22.653
[automatic door opening]

14:31.996 --> 14:33.539
[music fades]

14:33.623 --> 14:35.124
What brings you here?

14:35.750 --> 14:37.752
You said you'd never come see me again.

14:39.003 --> 14:40.797
Are you still upset with me?

14:40.880 --> 14:42.799
[chuckles] Am I upset?

14:43.674 --> 14:45.927
Why would I feel anything towards you?

14:46.594 --> 14:47.678
Get to the point.

14:47.762 --> 14:50.556
I'm a busy person.
Why did you want to see me?

14:51.724 --> 14:53.309
I came to ask a favor.

14:54.727 --> 14:58.231
We're not exactly on good enough terms
to be asking for favors, are we?

15:03.694 --> 15:05.655
I'd like you to take on a case for me.

15:06.823 --> 15:09.117
You know my classmate, Yu Mi-rae, right?

15:09.200 --> 15:11.661
The sexual harassment case
that was dropped before.

15:11.744 --> 15:13.996
She has officially filed
a report this time.

15:15.164 --> 15:18.835
You're the one who caused this mess,
so you should be the one to fix it.

15:18.918 --> 15:21.462
Why don't you handle it yourself?
Why are you asking me?

15:21.546 --> 15:24.424
Didn't you leave because
you didn't want to be a lawyer like me?

15:27.051 --> 15:28.136
I know…

15:30.179 --> 15:32.515
you would've handled
the recent case the same way,

15:32.598 --> 15:34.976
whether your opponent
was me or someone else.

15:35.685 --> 15:37.854
You're someone who wins
by any means necessary.

15:37.937 --> 15:40.648
Someone who will make the bully suffer
many times over.

15:41.441 --> 15:44.068
I want her to have
a lawyer like that in my place.

15:46.112 --> 15:47.405
And that's you.

15:50.950 --> 15:52.493
I get why you're asking me.

15:54.620 --> 15:56.873
But why do you think
I'd do this favor for you?

15:56.956 --> 15:58.374
Because you like me.

15:59.083 --> 15:59.959
What?

16:00.042 --> 16:03.337
You never waste your time
on something you're not interested in.

16:03.421 --> 16:06.382
You wouldn't meet just anyone
who came looking for you.

16:06.466 --> 16:08.259
You're busy with big cases,

16:08.342 --> 16:10.303
but you still took
the Rosa Restaurant case.

16:11.053 --> 16:13.097
Wasn't that because you feel
a certain way towards me,

16:13.181 --> 16:16.100
whether that's hating me
or something else?

16:16.184 --> 16:18.269
[soft pensive music playing]

16:18.352 --> 16:20.938
Wouldn't most people see that as bullying?

16:21.022 --> 16:23.191
You're not like most people, though.

16:25.860 --> 16:28.237
Please, sir.

16:36.162 --> 16:39.040
You still haven't told me
why you're not taking this case.

16:39.999 --> 16:41.167
What's going on?

16:42.919 --> 16:43.961
It's just…

16:45.046 --> 16:46.339
a personal reason.

16:47.131 --> 16:49.383
So it's none of my business? [scoffs]

16:49.467 --> 16:55.014
You told me that my weakness
makes me stronger and more special.

16:59.519 --> 17:03.231
And yet you seem to have no intention
of showing your weakness.

17:05.900 --> 17:06.901
Or…

17:08.152 --> 17:09.612
maybe that's your weakness.

17:15.076 --> 17:16.160
Thank you.

17:24.377 --> 17:26.379
[music fades]

17:30.007 --> 17:32.134
We're done with the guardian registration.

17:33.803 --> 17:37.181
You won't have to worry about
your identity or inheritance anymore.

17:37.723 --> 17:40.893
Is there anything else you need,
or do you have any questions?

17:45.189 --> 17:47.358
Please take a look at this for me.

17:47.441 --> 17:49.068
ROSA RESTAURANT

17:50.528 --> 17:53.447
Mi-ji drew these.
Which one do you think looks best?

17:53.531 --> 17:55.700
ROSA RESTAURANT
ONLY THE CHICKEN AND ROSA WILL BE LIT UP

17:58.869 --> 18:01.497
This one looks most
like a real restaurant sign, doesn't it?

18:03.416 --> 18:04.417
They all look great.

18:07.503 --> 18:11.882
I can't believe I'm worrying
about such trivial matters now.

18:14.760 --> 18:16.053
Ma'am.

18:17.430 --> 18:20.933
If you need any help
with the adult adoption we discussed,

18:21.017 --> 18:23.311
or if you need any legal assistance…

18:23.394 --> 18:24.312
HWANG JI-SU

18:24.395 --> 18:26.355
…you can contact this person
from now on.

18:26.439 --> 18:29.692
I've already spoken to her,
so she'll gladly help you if you call.

18:31.152 --> 18:32.028
[exhales]

18:32.653 --> 18:36.657
I must have taken up a lot of your time,
considering how busy you are.

18:36.741 --> 18:40.995
I asked you to help me with everything
because I can't do anything by myself.

18:41.078 --> 18:42.788
No, it's not that.

18:44.165 --> 18:47.418
It's just that I won't be able
to see you for a while.

18:48.794 --> 18:50.421
Why? Did something happen?

18:51.213 --> 18:52.798
It's just a personal…

18:56.594 --> 18:58.596
[soft melancholic music playing]

18:58.679 --> 18:59.722
To be honest…

19:01.432 --> 19:02.808
I'm a little sick.

19:02.892 --> 19:05.269
You're sick? Where? How?

19:05.895 --> 19:07.980
It's not very serious. It's just…

19:08.064 --> 19:10.399
What is it? Just tell me.

19:10.483 --> 19:11.984
Are you very sick?

19:14.945 --> 19:16.072
You…

19:18.157 --> 19:20.409
don't have cancer, do you?

19:22.411 --> 19:24.914
Why aren't you saying anything?
Is it cancer?

19:26.332 --> 19:27.917
It's nothing serious.

19:30.920 --> 19:33.005
I just have a problem with my ear.

19:34.507 --> 19:35.508
Your ear?

19:36.926 --> 19:39.679
You told me that your hearing
isn't great in one ear.

19:39.762 --> 19:41.222
Has it gotten worse?

19:42.264 --> 19:44.892
My hearing in the other ear
has become worse.

19:45.518 --> 19:47.186
Phone calls are difficult
for me right now.

19:47.269 --> 19:48.854
That's why I told you to contact her.

19:48.938 --> 19:50.773
You haven't taken up my time at all.

19:52.358 --> 19:53.776
Have you told Mi-ji?

19:55.903 --> 19:56.987
No.

19:58.072 --> 19:59.699
I haven't decided yet.

20:00.366 --> 20:01.742
Decided what?

20:01.826 --> 20:05.287
You haven't decided
whether to tell her or not?

20:06.580 --> 20:07.957
I don't know…

20:09.709 --> 20:11.794
what would be better for Mi-ji.

20:11.877 --> 20:14.755
Regardless of what would be better,
you can't hide this from her.

20:14.839 --> 20:17.369
It's not like you'll never see her again.

20:17.466 --> 20:18.634
I haven't decided…

20:20.052 --> 20:21.512
what to do about that either.

20:22.346 --> 20:23.347
Is…

20:24.098 --> 20:25.683
your condition that serious?

20:26.475 --> 20:27.685
No, it's not.

20:28.227 --> 20:31.313
Anyway, don't worry too much
if you can't get a hold of me.

20:32.064 --> 20:33.357
And please…

20:33.441 --> 20:34.567
[inhales deeply]

20:35.443 --> 20:36.902
…don't tell Mi-ji.

20:36.986 --> 20:39.947
If you were able to tell me,
why are you hiding it from her?

20:40.030 --> 20:44.326
Mi-ji would never change her mind
about you just because you're sick.

20:44.410 --> 20:45.703
That's exactly why.

20:48.122 --> 20:49.749
As you already know…

20:51.625 --> 20:54.128
it's not easy to be there
for someone who's sick.

20:56.505 --> 20:58.924
Mi-ji is just starting
to spread her wings again.

21:01.218 --> 21:03.345
[trembling] I don't want to hold her back.

21:06.599 --> 21:08.309
So this is about how you feel,

21:09.643 --> 21:12.271
not how Mi-ji feels.

21:15.775 --> 21:16.901
[Sang-wol sighs]

21:20.946 --> 21:22.156
GWANGHWAMUN

21:22.239 --> 21:24.241
[soft melancholic music continues]

21:26.619 --> 21:28.913
[Bun-hong's sister]
It's not like he's even healthy.

21:28.996 --> 21:31.916
You'll have to take care of him
his whole life.

21:31.999 --> 21:34.168
Why take on that burden?

21:35.795 --> 21:37.087
[footsteps approaching]

21:37.171 --> 21:39.173
[music fades]

21:43.677 --> 21:45.137
Are you still sick?

21:46.263 --> 21:47.431
No.

21:47.515 --> 21:51.143
Be honest while you still have the chance.
I don't want us fighting again.

21:51.227 --> 21:52.269
I'm really okay.

21:52.937 --> 21:54.230
You're okay?

21:55.272 --> 21:56.524
Then you deserve a punch.

21:57.066 --> 22:00.611
Do you know how upset I was yesterday?

22:01.111 --> 22:03.989
You seemed mad that I went
to your place without telling you.

22:04.073 --> 22:06.492
And then you didn't even
call me after that.

22:07.701 --> 22:08.869
I'm sorry.

22:09.370 --> 22:10.454
Jeez.

22:11.705 --> 22:15.793
If we keep going straight like this
and then make a slight right turn…

22:16.418 --> 22:17.503
It's…

22:18.087 --> 22:20.005
Ah, I found
another good restaurant nearby.

22:20.089 --> 22:21.882
Let's go there.

22:21.966 --> 22:24.301
I'm okay. Let's just stick
to where we were going.

22:24.385 --> 22:27.388
It's not that. I'm suddenly craving
something greasy.

22:27.471 --> 22:28.597
I mean it.

22:28.681 --> 22:32.393
Hold on. I'm going to go check
where we're going. I'll be right back.

22:32.476 --> 22:34.353
It's, uh…

22:40.317 --> 22:42.862
[soft melancholic music playing]

22:43.779 --> 22:46.282
[young Ho-su panting]

22:58.419 --> 23:00.963
I wonder if ghosts appear at night
at Gyeongbokgung Palace.

23:01.046 --> 23:02.923
[muffled] It was built a long time ago,

23:03.007 --> 23:05.301
so tons of people
must've died there over the years.

23:05.384 --> 23:06.552
Some were executed by poison.

23:06.635 --> 23:09.638
[clearly] No, wait.
Was the poison delivered to their homes?

23:09.722 --> 23:11.640
Anyway, I'm so excited.

23:11.724 --> 23:13.392
[giggles] Ta-da.

23:16.770 --> 23:18.355
[footsteps approaching]

23:19.064 --> 23:20.649
[server] Pardon me.

23:23.527 --> 23:26.322
I don't think we ordered this.

23:26.405 --> 23:28.532
We ran out of ingredients, so earlier,

23:28.616 --> 23:30.618
you said it was okay
to switch to this dish.

23:30.701 --> 23:32.661
You're right. Yes, that's right.

23:33.203 --> 23:35.205
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

23:37.374 --> 23:39.752
You weren't listening earlier, were you?

23:39.835 --> 23:44.006
I was wondering why you ordered this
when you don't even like clams that much.

23:44.089 --> 23:46.592
No, just eat what you ordered. It's okay.

23:46.675 --> 23:48.302
No, I like this too.

23:48.385 --> 23:51.472
Let's eat quickly and go,
so we're not late for the entry time.

23:53.223 --> 23:54.934
This looks delicious.

23:55.017 --> 23:57.728
- [cutlery clinking]
- [soft melancholic music continues]

24:22.670 --> 24:25.881
[Mi-ji] Did you know that the palace
isn't always open at night?

24:25.965 --> 24:28.384
Tickets were sold out
when I tried to book them,

24:28.467 --> 24:30.177
so I kept checking all night

24:30.260 --> 24:32.262
and I finally managed
to get some canceled tickets.

24:32.346 --> 24:33.555
[music fades]

24:33.639 --> 24:35.015
Hey.

24:35.099 --> 24:37.351
Are you really okay?
You don't look too good.

24:37.434 --> 24:38.435
Should we go another day?

24:39.353 --> 24:41.271
No, really, I'm fine.

24:41.939 --> 24:45.317
No, let's just cancel.
We can always go another day.

24:45.401 --> 24:46.694
I told you, I'm fine.

24:46.777 --> 24:48.904
We can just book tickets again.

24:48.988 --> 24:52.116
I know how to book them now, so…

24:52.199 --> 24:53.701
- Mi-ji.
- [Mi-ji] Yes?

24:57.454 --> 24:58.956
Let's stop seeing each other.

25:01.375 --> 25:02.418
[chuckles] Jeez.

25:02.501 --> 25:04.962
What are you talking about?

25:08.382 --> 25:11.301
Do you really mean what you just said?

25:11.385 --> 25:13.387
I've been thinking about it for a while.

25:15.014 --> 25:16.557
I feel like we're just too different.

25:17.433 --> 25:20.102
[exhales] You knew we were different.

25:20.602 --> 25:23.939
Dating's about two different people
adjusting to each other…

25:24.023 --> 25:25.858
You can only adjust so much, though.

25:28.110 --> 25:31.321
The way we live and think
will keep changing more and more.

25:31.405 --> 25:32.990
Before it gets too hard--

25:33.073 --> 25:35.367
Do you really expect me
to believe you right now?

25:35.451 --> 25:39.496
Did you really think I'd say,
"Gosh. Yes, we're too different"?

25:40.080 --> 25:42.041
You told me to stop doubting myself.

25:42.124 --> 25:45.753
Did you think I would fall for this
when you told me that over and over?

25:45.836 --> 25:48.338
Tell me. What's going on?

25:48.422 --> 25:51.133
You would never do something like this
out of the blue.

25:56.221 --> 25:57.222
I…

25:59.308 --> 26:01.310
I'm having issues with this ear too.

26:02.227 --> 26:04.855
- [Mi-ji] What?
- They said I have sudden hearing loss.

26:05.689 --> 26:08.650
I don't know if my hearing
will get better or worse.

26:08.734 --> 26:09.860
When did it start?

26:10.694 --> 26:14.198
Don't tell me
it was that time you said someone died…

26:14.281 --> 26:16.992
It's been bad since then,
so I've been getting treated.

26:18.494 --> 26:21.955
But even if it gets better,
my hearing won't be the same anymore.

26:22.039 --> 26:23.165
If I'm unlucky…

26:25.042 --> 26:26.418
I may lose my hearing completely.

26:28.921 --> 26:30.005
So?

26:30.089 --> 26:32.341
What does that have to do
with us breaking up right now?

26:32.424 --> 26:34.510
You think I'll change
because you can't hear anymore?

26:34.593 --> 26:35.803
I'll change.

26:36.929 --> 26:38.931
I'll have trouble talking on the phone.

26:39.556 --> 26:42.434
At some point, we may not even
be able to talk like we do now.

26:42.518 --> 26:45.354
Then I can adjust to that.

26:45.437 --> 26:48.398
I'll do whatever I can.
I'll learn sign language if I have to.

26:48.482 --> 26:51.777
I'll talk to you all day
just like we do now.

26:51.860 --> 26:52.986
That's why I'm doing this.

26:54.571 --> 26:56.365
[pensive music playing]

26:56.448 --> 26:58.992
You've been compromising
for me all this time.

26:59.076 --> 27:01.245
I don't want you
to have to do that anymore.

27:01.328 --> 27:04.289
Hey! I want to do that, though.

27:04.373 --> 27:08.919
I'm doing it because I want to.
Why do you care?

27:11.088 --> 27:13.173
- Mi-ji.
- [breathes shakily]

27:13.757 --> 27:15.050
[Ho-su] You know…

27:17.094 --> 27:19.012
how I feel, though.

27:21.265 --> 27:22.724
You went through it, so you know.

27:26.353 --> 27:27.938
[pensive music continues]

27:28.021 --> 27:30.149
[young Mi-ji] Now I get why you acted out.

27:31.984 --> 27:33.402
Being pitied…

27:34.611 --> 27:36.238
feels like crap.

27:38.615 --> 27:39.658
[exhales]

27:41.869 --> 27:43.620
[breathes heavily]

27:43.704 --> 27:47.082
I guess I haven't matured much
over the years.

27:48.333 --> 27:51.587
I don't want you to see me getting worse.

27:51.670 --> 27:54.131
I'm already overwhelmed,
so I don't think I'll be able to handle

27:54.214 --> 27:56.675
seeing you have a hard time because of me.

27:56.758 --> 27:59.761
I know it's stupid to think that,
but that's just how I feel.

28:00.846 --> 28:02.264
Let's just end things here.

28:02.764 --> 28:04.308
[voice trembling] Ho-su.

28:05.350 --> 28:08.979
Ho-su, your life isn't over
just because you can't hear anymore.

28:09.062 --> 28:11.315
Just because you can't run anymore,
your life is over?

28:11.398 --> 28:12.774
It's true, isn't it?

28:12.858 --> 28:16.236
You never paid any attention to me
before I started running.

28:16.320 --> 28:17.404
I can't run anymore.

28:17.487 --> 28:20.407
My ankle's wrecked, and my life's ruined.

28:22.576 --> 28:23.577
I know.

28:24.369 --> 28:26.622
That's why I'm saying
that we should end things.

28:26.705 --> 28:28.832
No, we don't know for sure yet.

28:28.916 --> 28:30.876
Your hearing could get better.

28:32.711 --> 28:35.172
Even the doctor said it's unlikely.
That's what he told me.

28:35.255 --> 28:36.673
- [hesitates]
- You'll get better.

28:36.757 --> 28:39.593
Are you a doctor?
How am I ever supposed to get better?

28:43.055 --> 28:44.264
[Ho-su] I'm really glad…

28:45.849 --> 28:47.601
that I got to know you, Mi-ji.

28:49.895 --> 28:50.896
Take care.

28:51.647 --> 28:55.734
Where are you going?
I refuse to end things like this.

28:55.817 --> 28:59.404
We can get through it together.
Ho-su, I'll help you.

28:59.488 --> 29:02.324
We've been doing great together.
So we can keep--

29:02.407 --> 29:04.034
So keep ignoring me.

29:04.117 --> 29:05.869
I'm just sitting here, dead quiet.

29:05.953 --> 29:07.871
So please leave me alone!

29:09.623 --> 29:11.208
We're done here, right?

29:11.291 --> 29:13.669
[music turns sorrowful]

29:15.837 --> 29:17.047
[sighs]

29:40.320 --> 29:41.321
[whimpers]

29:42.781 --> 29:43.865
Wha…

29:45.701 --> 29:46.910
[whimpers]

29:56.378 --> 29:58.505
[door lock beeps, chimes]

29:58.588 --> 30:00.424
- [door opens]
- [music fades]

30:00.507 --> 30:02.342
You're back earlier than I expected.

30:02.426 --> 30:03.385
[door lock chimes]

30:04.177 --> 30:06.263
Is everything okay with Ho-su?

30:06.346 --> 30:09.433
He told me he'd introduce me
to another lawyer out of nowhere.

30:24.156 --> 30:25.866
Did something happen?

30:27.075 --> 30:28.535
We broke up.

30:29.453 --> 30:30.537
What?

30:31.163 --> 30:34.082
What? Why? Did Ho-su break up with you?

30:36.418 --> 30:37.919
Are you okay?

30:39.755 --> 30:41.715
I should've stopped him.

30:43.300 --> 30:44.760
But I couldn't.

30:46.136 --> 30:47.512
[melancholic pop song playing]

30:47.596 --> 30:51.725
I get why he's doing this, but…

30:53.268 --> 30:54.394
I really…

30:55.729 --> 30:58.106
get why, but…

30:59.816 --> 31:00.734
[hesitates]

31:01.485 --> 31:04.863
[voice trembling] But I didn't know
what to say to change his mind.

31:07.949 --> 31:08.992
So…

31:11.870 --> 31:13.538
I couldn't stop him.

31:15.874 --> 31:17.167
I let him go.

31:20.128 --> 31:22.464
I couldn't stop him, and I let him go.

31:22.547 --> 31:25.342
[melancholic pop song continues]

31:27.552 --> 31:28.470
[sobs]

31:30.764 --> 31:33.350
[continues sobbing]

31:33.433 --> 31:37.771
[singing in Korean]

31:41.358 --> 31:45.487
[singing in Korean continues]

31:45.570 --> 31:47.155
What am I going to do?

31:48.365 --> 31:50.409
[Mi-ji sobbing]

31:54.413 --> 31:55.414
[door lock beeping]

31:55.497 --> 31:57.374
- [door opens]
- [melancholic pop song continues]

31:57.457 --> 31:58.375
[door closes]

32:01.086 --> 32:05.549
[singing in Korean]

32:07.259 --> 32:08.135
[lamp clicks]

32:08.218 --> 32:11.096
[singing in Korean continues]

32:11.179 --> 32:12.305
[Ho-su sighs]

32:13.014 --> 32:14.683
[cell phone buzzes]

32:17.394 --> 32:20.522
[singing in Korean]

32:23.775 --> 32:30.157
[singing in Korean continues]

32:31.324 --> 32:32.742
[exhales deeply]

32:35.036 --> 32:36.455
[exhales]

32:39.207 --> 32:40.333
[sobs]

32:42.627 --> 32:44.254
Damn it.

32:45.297 --> 32:47.591
[in English] ♪ Would you ever come? ♪

32:50.844 --> 32:55.849
- [sniffles, sobs]
- [singing in Korean]

32:56.391 --> 32:59.895
- [Ho-su whimpers]
- [singing in Korean continues]

33:00.770 --> 33:03.690
[song concludes]

33:03.773 --> 33:06.234
- [birds chirping]
- [Mi-ji in Korean] Hey, Mi-rae.

33:06.943 --> 33:10.030
You still have time, right?
Eat something before you go.

33:14.743 --> 33:16.453
Why are you up at this hour?

33:17.120 --> 33:19.164
You're turning in your resignation today.

33:19.247 --> 33:21.082
I figured you should have
a good breakfast.

33:21.166 --> 33:22.417
[Mi-ji clears throat]

33:22.918 --> 33:25.295
I'm sorry that I've been moping around
the past few days.

33:25.378 --> 33:27.130
Why are you apologizing for that?

33:27.214 --> 33:30.717
It's annoying to be around someone
who's all sad and depressed.

33:30.800 --> 33:34.513
I know you already have
a lot to worry about.

33:35.931 --> 33:38.767
It's way better than seeing you
pretend to be all cheerful.

33:38.850 --> 33:39.851
Hey.

33:40.560 --> 33:41.686
It's a rabbit.

33:44.022 --> 33:44.940
Jeez.

33:51.112 --> 33:54.115
Ho-su's not answering my calls.
Have you tried calling him?

33:56.284 --> 33:57.369
No.

33:59.871 --> 34:02.874
What do you plan on doing now?

34:03.375 --> 34:07.462
I got this apartment with a company loan,
so I need to move out as soon as I quit.

34:08.088 --> 34:11.633
If you're going to stay in Seoul,
you'll have to look for a place to stay.

34:12.259 --> 34:13.802
Are you going to stay in Seoul?

34:16.429 --> 34:17.597
I'll think about it.

34:19.641 --> 34:23.144
After I clear out my desk, I'm going
to Duson-ri tomorrow. Do you want to come?

34:23.228 --> 34:26.147
No, it's okay. Why would I go
when you're going to go talk to Mom?

34:31.027 --> 34:32.821
When I go home,

34:33.655 --> 34:35.448
do you want me to fix it?

34:36.533 --> 34:37.784
Your doorknob.

34:39.703 --> 34:42.414
It's okay. I'll take care of it later.

34:44.249 --> 34:46.418
[melancholic music playing]

35:01.308 --> 35:02.976
[doorbell ringing]

35:03.059 --> 35:04.102
[sighs]

35:07.188 --> 35:08.481
Who is it?

35:09.316 --> 35:10.609
[music fades]

35:12.485 --> 35:13.653
[door lock chimes]

35:15.488 --> 35:17.574
Hey! Gyeong-gu!

35:17.657 --> 35:19.242
There's no time to explain.

35:19.326 --> 35:22.120
Put on as many layers as you can
and then come out.

35:22.203 --> 35:23.538
Go!

35:29.461 --> 35:30.837
[camera clicking]

35:33.006 --> 35:34.090
Mm.

35:36.760 --> 35:39.429
You should've told me
that you two switched back.

35:39.512 --> 35:41.264
I had no idea, so I contacted Mi-rae.

35:41.348 --> 35:43.475
Do you know how awkward it was?

35:44.225 --> 35:46.603
There are even more people here now.
[grunts excitedly]

35:46.686 --> 35:48.021
Are you happy?

35:48.521 --> 35:51.775
Do you really want to stand in line
in this weather just to buy shoes?

35:51.858 --> 35:53.526
They're not just sneakers.

35:53.610 --> 35:55.904
They're limited edition.

35:55.987 --> 35:57.656
When are we going in?

35:57.739 --> 35:59.616
Want to know something shocking?

35:59.699 --> 36:03.578
We're in line to get into
another line right now. [grunts]

36:03.662 --> 36:05.246
Unbelievable. I'm leaving.

36:05.330 --> 36:06.706
- No, you can't.
- [groans]

36:06.790 --> 36:10.126
It's limited to one pair per person.
I have to get one in every color.

36:10.210 --> 36:11.252
[Mi-ji] I knew it.

36:11.336 --> 36:15.131
I thought it was strange that you'd come
all this way just to see me.

36:15.215 --> 36:19.177
Jeez, I'm just killing
two birds with one stone.

36:19.803 --> 36:22.889
Hey, what's Ho-su doing?
Tell him to come here if he's not busy.

36:22.972 --> 36:24.641
Why do you want him to come?

36:24.724 --> 36:26.309
[Gyeong-gu] Just multitasking, you know?

36:26.393 --> 36:28.645
Call him so I can buy three pairs.
Come on!

36:28.728 --> 36:30.146
Get lost.

36:30.230 --> 36:33.024
Look at you,
being all protective of your boyfriend.

36:33.650 --> 36:35.902
Hey, in a winter as cold as this,

36:35.985 --> 36:39.239
you need to get out and face the cold.
It's better for your health.

36:39.322 --> 36:40.281
Don't do it.

36:40.365 --> 36:42.492
Let me see that handsome face of his.

36:42.992 --> 36:45.829
I'll be the unhappy third wheel, not you.

36:46.413 --> 36:48.540
I said, don't!

36:49.416 --> 36:51.418
Why are you yelling?

36:53.420 --> 36:55.130
Did something happen between you two?

36:56.089 --> 36:58.842
- [camera clicks]
- [soft pop music playing over speakers]

37:02.595 --> 37:04.931
What is up with Ho-su?

37:05.014 --> 37:06.641
Does he think he's that great?

37:07.350 --> 37:09.853
Why did he mess around
with someone who's never dated before?

37:09.936 --> 37:11.604
Come on.

37:12.105 --> 37:14.190
I told you
that we both agreed to break up.

37:14.274 --> 37:16.568
[scoffs] You agreed?

37:16.651 --> 37:19.195
Are you sure about that?
Your eyes are full of longing right now.

37:19.279 --> 37:21.448
You were obviously dumped.

37:23.032 --> 37:25.493
What did he say?
Did he say you're too stupid for him

37:25.577 --> 37:27.912
or you're pathetic
because you're unemployed?

37:28.538 --> 37:30.707
He said you turned out
to be a bit annoying, right?

37:30.790 --> 37:33.793
Hey, that's a bit harsh.

37:33.877 --> 37:35.378
You went through all that drama,

37:35.462 --> 37:38.173
but you didn't even last a year.
What was the point of dating, then?

37:38.256 --> 37:41.593
Why did he come and stir things up
when you were doing fine on your own?

37:41.676 --> 37:44.137
Yu Candy looks
totally messed up right now.

37:44.220 --> 37:46.931
Hey, let's just ambush him tonight.

37:47.015 --> 37:50.059
I'll lure Ho-su.
You attack him from the back.

37:50.935 --> 37:53.313
So I'm the one who's supposed
to hit him, not you?

37:54.355 --> 37:55.440
Jeez.

37:58.526 --> 38:02.489
This is why first loves
should just be kept as memories.

38:03.865 --> 38:07.202
You regret it too, don't you?
You wish you hadn't dated him, right?

38:08.119 --> 38:09.120
No.

38:10.413 --> 38:11.873
I don't regret it.

38:14.167 --> 38:16.294
I'm glad I dated Ho-su.

38:29.724 --> 38:30.809
[cell phone beeps]

38:36.731 --> 38:38.191
"No, I don't regret it."

38:38.274 --> 38:40.318
Can you repeat what you said,
starting from that line?

38:40.401 --> 38:41.903
You showed great emotion just now.

38:41.986 --> 38:43.029
[in English] Action!

38:43.530 --> 38:45.949
[in Korean] Jeez!
Do you seriously have a death wish?

38:46.032 --> 38:47.408
- Just once.
- This is insured, right?

38:47.492 --> 38:48.409
I'm breaking it.

38:48.493 --> 38:51.538
Even cringey moments are a part
of your history. We need to document this.

38:51.621 --> 38:54.082
I can't believe
I waited with you in the cold.

38:54.165 --> 38:56.334
- Jeez.
- [Gyeong-gu] Hey, watch the shoes!

38:56.417 --> 38:58.419
[sighs, groans]

38:58.503 --> 39:00.046
My shoes!

39:02.048 --> 39:03.883
[cell phone buzzing]

39:07.053 --> 39:08.054
Hello?

39:08.137 --> 39:09.681
[nurse] I'm calling from the hospital.

39:09.764 --> 39:11.391
Are you Ms. Kang Wol-sun's daughter?

39:11.474 --> 39:12.851
Yes. Is there a problem?

39:13.935 --> 39:15.353
[kids chattering]

39:15.436 --> 39:17.272
I'm sorry. Hold on. Be careful. Sorry!

39:17.355 --> 39:20.066
Gosh, Ms. Kim.
Don't run in front of the children…

39:20.149 --> 39:21.568
Where are you going?

39:21.651 --> 39:23.444
- [Wol-sun] Honey!
- [nurse] It's okay, ma'am.

39:23.528 --> 39:26.197
- Ma'am, it's okay.
- [Wol-sun] Stop! Honey!

39:26.281 --> 39:27.574
- Honey!
- [nurse] It's okay.

39:27.657 --> 39:30.285
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!

39:30.368 --> 39:32.412
[Wol-sun wails] Honey…

39:32.495 --> 39:33.746
What's wrong with my mom?

39:33.830 --> 39:35.540
She's had diarrhea for the past few days.

39:35.623 --> 39:37.959
I think she's delirious
from sodium deficiency.

39:38.459 --> 39:40.044
Fortunately, it's not an infection.

39:40.128 --> 39:42.297
It's because she hasn't been eating
as much lately.

39:42.380 --> 39:45.675
So she'll get a little better
once she gets a sodium infusion.

39:45.758 --> 39:49.554
She's blabbering nonsense, though.
Do you think an IV will be enough?

39:49.637 --> 39:52.640
For delirium, the most important thing
is to keep the patient calm and stable.

39:52.724 --> 39:57.103
You should hold her hand
and keep talking to her.

39:57.186 --> 39:59.355
- [whimpers]
- [Ok-hui] Mom.

39:59.439 --> 40:01.441
- Mom.
- Why would you hit her?

40:01.524 --> 40:06.070
Hit me! Why would you hit our kid?

40:06.154 --> 40:09.782
- [soft pensive music playing]
- Why are you hitting Ok-hui?

40:10.533 --> 40:13.077
Mom, I'm here. It's me.

40:13.161 --> 40:15.038
I'm Ok-hui. I'm here, Mom.

40:15.121 --> 40:18.625
You shouldn't do that either, Mother.

40:18.708 --> 40:22.462
Our child did nothing wrong.
My poor baby.

40:23.004 --> 40:24.547
[Wol-sun sobbing]

40:25.173 --> 40:26.257
My baby.

40:37.894 --> 40:39.646
[music fades]

40:49.614 --> 40:51.616
HIDDEN TRUTHS ABOUT HEARING LOSS

40:51.699 --> 40:54.577
HOW TO RESET TINNITUS
AND HEARING LOSS

41:22.772 --> 41:25.191
[melancholic music playing]

41:30.196 --> 41:34.492
[Ho-su] I wonder if this is the moment
Dad was talking about.

41:37.370 --> 41:38.788
Ho-su.

41:39.372 --> 41:41.332
Doesn't your neck hurt?

41:41.874 --> 41:42.917
[chuckles]

41:43.751 --> 41:46.087
I guess this attitude
is typical of an eighth grader.

41:46.170 --> 41:49.465
You're not even responding.
I'm going to tell your mom later.

41:49.549 --> 41:50.425
Which mom?

41:56.848 --> 41:57.849
Ho-su.

41:59.559 --> 42:02.145
Someday, you're going
to make someone miserable too.

42:04.897 --> 42:08.192
There will definitely be a moment

42:08.276 --> 42:10.778
when you force the person
by your side to lose.

42:10.862 --> 42:12.196
But you know, Ho-su…

42:13.156 --> 42:16.659
Love isn't about winning or losing.
It's about--

42:16.743 --> 42:17.910
[tires squeal]

42:20.121 --> 42:22.790
[Ho-su] I wonder what Dad
was going to say after that.

42:23.750 --> 42:26.169
His ominous prediction came true.

42:27.128 --> 42:29.047
He never got to finish his sentence.

42:32.759 --> 42:34.594
I'll never know…

42:35.511 --> 42:37.096
the end of that sentence…

42:38.514 --> 42:39.891
or love itself.

42:39.974 --> 42:41.559
[music fades]

42:49.692 --> 42:52.695
[Mi-ji] Wow! [giggles]

42:52.779 --> 42:55.239
- It's beautiful.
- [camera shutter clicking]

42:55.323 --> 42:56.324
[gasps]

42:57.533 --> 43:00.620
Okay, selfie time.

43:04.457 --> 43:05.792
What?

43:05.875 --> 43:09.045
Is this your first time
seeing the Hangang River or something?

43:15.968 --> 43:18.221
Nothing beats chicken and beer
by the Hangang River, right?

43:18.304 --> 43:21.099
[Mi-ji] You always want to do
what everyone else is doing.

43:21.182 --> 43:24.477
Do you really want to eat
chicken and beer outside in this weather?

43:24.560 --> 43:28.397
The colder it is, the better it tastes.
You act as if you're not gonna have some.

43:28.481 --> 43:29.857
I'm not eating.

43:30.691 --> 43:31.776
Fine, don't eat.

43:32.276 --> 43:35.238
A broken heart is great for dieting.

43:36.322 --> 43:37.406
Hey.

43:38.658 --> 43:40.159
Stop moping around.

43:40.701 --> 43:42.537
Eat this and come back home with me.

43:43.412 --> 43:44.539
No, thanks.

43:45.164 --> 43:47.125
What do you mean?

43:47.208 --> 43:50.253
You said that
you can't even live with Mi-rae.

43:50.336 --> 43:52.839
In Seoul, just breathing costs money.

43:52.922 --> 43:55.550
Don't waste money
and just come back with me.

43:56.509 --> 43:59.428
Go back by yourself.
I'm going to stay here.

44:00.179 --> 44:02.807
You've always liked Seoul
since we were in high school. Why is that?

44:02.890 --> 44:05.059
If you're gonna mope around,
do it back home.

44:05.143 --> 44:06.894
You'll at least have your family and me.

44:06.978 --> 44:09.814
If you mope around here,
you'll shut yourself away again…

44:16.404 --> 44:17.697
Damn it.

44:22.910 --> 44:25.163
Who's going to
pull you back out if you do?

44:26.247 --> 44:28.916
I refuse to stand by
and watch you die alone in Seoul.

44:35.464 --> 44:36.841
Why are you making that face?

44:40.344 --> 44:43.890
I've been thinking about something
the past few days.

44:45.933 --> 44:48.477
If I could go back in time,

44:49.520 --> 44:52.440
what would I have to say

44:52.523 --> 44:54.442
to convince myself to leave the room?

44:57.028 --> 44:58.779
But I don't know what I would say.

45:00.198 --> 45:01.699
I thought about it,

45:02.950 --> 45:05.536
and I realized
that I didn't leave of my own accord.

45:08.706 --> 45:09.665
I stayed in that room,

45:09.749 --> 45:12.501
thinking I was the only one
going through a hard time.

45:12.585 --> 45:14.879
I never thought about
what it must've been like

45:14.962 --> 45:16.714
for those watching me from outside.

45:19.217 --> 45:23.846
I wonder what was going through
my mom's mind when she broke my doorknob.

45:24.472 --> 45:28.517
Just how much do you have to love someone
to say it's all okay

45:29.185 --> 45:31.938
despite everything, like my grandma did?

45:32.688 --> 45:34.607
[gentle music playing]

45:34.690 --> 45:37.485
Mi-rae couldn't even talk
about her own struggles.

45:38.778 --> 45:40.863
She must've been so lonely.

45:42.156 --> 45:43.741
[inhales deeply]

45:43.824 --> 45:45.701
And what is Gyeong-gu thinking

45:46.661 --> 45:50.831
as he sits and eats chicken
here at this hour

45:51.415 --> 45:52.875
while facing this strong wind?

45:56.045 --> 45:57.213
Jeez.

45:58.422 --> 46:02.218
I managed to leave my room,
thanks to all of you who cared about me.

46:02.718 --> 46:04.887
So I can't possibly go back in there.

46:05.680 --> 46:07.682
[inhales deeply]

46:07.765 --> 46:10.476
No matter how small I feel
or how hard things get,

46:11.769 --> 46:13.479
I'll do whatever I can here.

46:14.522 --> 46:16.023
I want to do all I can.…

46:17.900 --> 46:21.988
to become the kind of person
who's always there for others too.

46:37.420 --> 46:40.673
Well, dating a lawyer has certainly
improved your way with words.

46:45.928 --> 46:48.723
You just low-key wiped
your hand here, didn't you?

46:48.806 --> 46:49.807
Of course not.

46:49.890 --> 46:51.517
[Mi-ji] You did!

46:51.600 --> 46:53.894
- I didn't.
- [Mi-ji] Jeez.

46:53.978 --> 46:55.688
Why did you wipe it on me?

46:55.771 --> 46:57.773
You're supposed to eat chicken
with your hands.

46:57.857 --> 46:58.899
[Mi-ji] You're so annoying.

47:01.819 --> 47:03.904
[music fades]

47:06.782 --> 47:08.451
[employee] She's finally leaving.

47:09.744 --> 47:12.747
Look at her just walking away by herself
after throwing a grenade.

47:14.081 --> 47:16.125
Tell them to get rid of that desk.

47:16.208 --> 47:18.294
There's no one here to sit there anymore.

47:30.514 --> 47:32.558
[Mi-rae] Please give this to Su-yeon.

47:46.781 --> 47:48.324
[elevator chimes]

48:01.253 --> 48:02.505
It was you, wasn't it?

48:04.256 --> 48:06.842
You're the only one
who'd do something like this.

48:06.926 --> 48:08.427
[tense music playing]

48:08.511 --> 48:10.221
Do you really think I'm the only one?

48:10.304 --> 48:11.931
[Tae-gwan]
You think it'll all go your way?

48:12.014 --> 48:14.975
You dragged the FTC into this.
How are you going to handle the fallout?

48:15.059 --> 48:17.978
I'm not the one who has to deal
with the fallout.

48:20.022 --> 48:22.691
Do you think it'll all be over
if you leave like this?

48:23.359 --> 48:25.945
I'll make sure that you never
step foot in this field again.

48:26.028 --> 48:29.865
You'll probably join some lame company
and cause the same kind of issues there.

48:33.786 --> 48:36.122
You'll always be the same wherever you go.

48:37.581 --> 48:41.085
I guess that's what scares you the most.

48:41.961 --> 48:42.837
What?

48:42.920 --> 48:45.089
- [elevator chimes]
- [music turns daring]

48:45.172 --> 48:46.173
Goodbye.

48:47.508 --> 48:49.176
Good luck with the investigation.

48:59.478 --> 49:00.646
[exhales]

49:01.939 --> 49:02.982
[card reader beeps]

49:03.065 --> 49:04.442
[music fades]

49:04.984 --> 49:06.152
[employee] Ms. Yu.

49:06.652 --> 49:07.820
Ms. Yu!

49:08.737 --> 49:09.989
Mi-rae!

49:12.908 --> 49:15.286
I think you left this behind…

49:15.369 --> 49:17.538
Oh… thank you.

49:19.039 --> 49:20.458
[employee] I…

49:22.501 --> 49:25.921
I'm sorry that I just sat back
and did nothing all this time.

49:27.673 --> 49:30.551
In today's meeting,
I'm going to tell them everything.

49:34.180 --> 49:36.891
[soft pensive music playing]

49:59.830 --> 50:01.665
[music fades]

50:01.749 --> 50:04.043
I'm glad it's nothing serious.

50:04.126 --> 50:05.628
Is your mother doing better?

50:06.295 --> 50:08.506
Yes, it got bad last night.

50:09.048 --> 50:11.133
But she's blabbering less than before.

50:11.634 --> 50:13.928
We didn't force her to eat
to avoid upsetting her stomach,

50:14.011 --> 50:15.763
but it actually made things worse.

50:15.846 --> 50:17.473
[Bun-hong] You didn't do it on purpose.

50:17.556 --> 50:18.933
Are you okay?

50:19.934 --> 50:22.811
I heard delirium is tougher
on the loved ones than the patient.

50:22.895 --> 50:25.356
She keeps talking about the past.

50:25.439 --> 50:27.566
Thanks to her, I'm reliving the past too.

50:28.442 --> 50:32.196
Anyway, I don't think I'll be able to work
until my mom gets better.

50:32.279 --> 50:34.073
[Bun-hong]
Work is not important right now.

50:34.156 --> 50:37.451
I'll take care of it,
so just focus on her for now.

50:38.786 --> 50:40.496
Okay, talk to you later.

50:43.999 --> 50:46.377
HNU ENT

50:51.215 --> 50:52.424
Hello?

50:53.425 --> 50:55.636
Doctor, I wasn't expecting
a call from you.

50:58.389 --> 51:00.349
Ho-su's phone is turned off?

51:01.392 --> 51:05.187
He probably had his regular checkup
over the summer, though.

51:10.484 --> 51:12.653
What are you talking about?

51:13.445 --> 51:15.573
Please explain so I can understand.

51:16.991 --> 51:18.325
[water trickles]

51:22.162 --> 51:23.205
Mom.

51:24.415 --> 51:25.583
Who am I?

51:27.126 --> 51:29.003
Ok-hui.

51:34.174 --> 51:36.135
[sniffles, clears throat]

51:42.725 --> 51:44.768
Why are you so skinny?

51:46.186 --> 51:48.772
Don't you know old folks die
if they stop eating?

51:49.773 --> 51:51.442
Were you seriously trying to die?

51:52.026 --> 51:53.944
Don't you even feel bad for the girls?

51:56.989 --> 51:58.157
Mom.

51:59.199 --> 52:01.035
Who am I?

52:01.118 --> 52:02.703
I asked you who I am.

52:02.786 --> 52:04.663
Stop asking me.

52:05.497 --> 52:06.624
[chuckles] Jeez…

52:07.958 --> 52:09.460
I guess you're finally back.

52:18.469 --> 52:20.137
Did Dad hit me?

52:21.847 --> 52:23.557
You were saying that all night.

52:23.641 --> 52:25.684
Is that why you left the house?

52:26.935 --> 52:28.354
[hesitates]

52:29.063 --> 52:31.065
[sighs, sniffles]

52:31.148 --> 52:33.150
Then why did you say Dad mistreated you?

52:33.734 --> 52:35.903
You said you were kicked out
for having a girl.

52:37.363 --> 52:38.447
I was afraid…

52:39.865 --> 52:42.409
that you'd go back to that house.

52:42.493 --> 52:43.744
[Ok-hui sighs]

52:46.997 --> 52:48.957
Then why were you so mean to me?

52:50.292 --> 52:52.628
I thought you got kicked out
because of me,

52:52.711 --> 52:55.297
so I thought that you resented me for it.

52:56.507 --> 52:58.676
My whole life, I…

53:00.928 --> 53:03.555
- [gentle music playing]
- I was afraid that you'd live like me.

53:03.639 --> 53:07.935
I wanted you to live a good life
on your own.

53:08.018 --> 53:10.479
How was I supposed to do that by myself?

53:12.272 --> 53:15.067
I've spent all this time
thinking I destroyed your life.

53:15.859 --> 53:17.903
So how was I supposed to live a good life?

53:19.321 --> 53:22.282
If you left for my sake,
then you should've told me.

53:22.366 --> 53:24.827
Was it really that hard
for you to tell me?

53:24.910 --> 53:27.579
Why keep it a secret for so long?
[sniffles]

53:27.663 --> 53:29.707
Look at us now.

53:30.791 --> 53:32.876
It's too late now.

53:40.759 --> 53:42.136
Ok-hui.

53:44.179 --> 53:45.389
I'm sorry.

53:50.811 --> 53:52.271
Why are you apologizing?

53:53.731 --> 53:56.511
Are you gonna leave us
now that you're at peace?

53:56.608 --> 53:58.110
Don't even think about it.

53:58.193 --> 54:00.028
I haven't forgiven you yet.

54:00.112 --> 54:01.530
[water trickles]

54:04.158 --> 54:07.411
I'm… sorry.

54:07.494 --> 54:09.997
I told you not to apologize.

54:10.706 --> 54:14.710
I told you to stop.
Why do you keep apologizing?

54:17.755 --> 54:19.631
[sobs]

54:25.304 --> 54:26.889
[Ok-hui continues sobbing]

54:32.728 --> 54:35.731
[Ok-hui continues sobbing]

54:45.032 --> 54:46.742
[music fades]

54:47.993 --> 54:51.413
[intense rumbling]

54:51.497 --> 54:54.625
- [door alarm ringing]
- [rumbling continues]

54:56.043 --> 54:58.629
- [rumbling continues]
- [alarm continues ringing]

55:00.422 --> 55:02.508
- [alarm stops]
- [door lock chimes]

55:04.176 --> 55:05.511
What's going on?

55:05.594 --> 55:07.387
So you were inside.

55:08.013 --> 55:09.431
He's your son, right?

55:13.435 --> 55:14.353
[sighs sharply]

55:19.942 --> 55:22.402
I was asleep
and I didn't know my phone was off.

55:22.486 --> 55:24.279
You didn't have to call the police.

55:28.075 --> 55:29.368
[Ho-su sighs]

55:35.958 --> 55:37.626
How long have you been like this?

55:38.585 --> 55:40.796
I've been too busy to clean,
so it's a mess.

55:40.879 --> 55:42.506
Why didn't you go to the hospital?

55:44.132 --> 55:45.384
I already know everything.

55:45.467 --> 55:47.177
Get dressed. We're going to the hospital.

55:47.261 --> 55:48.929
I'll go on my own later.

55:49.012 --> 55:52.266
[sternly] You'll manage on your own?
Is that what you've been doing?

55:52.349 --> 55:53.350
[Ho-su] Mom.

55:54.142 --> 55:56.144
You don't have a terminal disease.

55:56.228 --> 55:58.146
It's sudden hearing loss.

55:58.230 --> 56:00.065
This is urgent.
Why aren't you doing anything?

56:00.148 --> 56:03.068
Do you think anything will change
if you hide away by yourself?

56:03.151 --> 56:05.821
You shouldn't avoid the problem.
You should take care of it.

56:05.904 --> 56:07.072
Avoid it?

56:07.990 --> 56:09.241
Me?

56:09.950 --> 56:12.369
Mom, I can't avoid it.

56:13.537 --> 56:15.706
I'm here like this
because I can't avoid it.

56:16.248 --> 56:17.833
I already went to the hospital.

56:19.251 --> 56:21.378
They said there's nothing they can do.

56:21.461 --> 56:23.380
They said all I can do is wait.

56:23.463 --> 56:25.090
I'm not avoiding anything.

56:26.842 --> 56:28.802
If there's a way to avoid it,

56:29.636 --> 56:31.638
I would love to know it too, Mom.

56:33.056 --> 56:35.559
Why did you let it get this bad
without telling me?

56:36.435 --> 56:39.313
You should've told me, of all people.

56:39.396 --> 56:41.231
You should've asked for my help.

56:42.566 --> 56:43.817
What are we?

56:45.277 --> 56:46.320
What?

56:47.029 --> 56:50.866
You've already done more than enough
by raising me all this time.

56:51.366 --> 56:54.786
You should stop worrying about me,
and you should live your own life now.

56:58.248 --> 56:59.791
What? I did more than enough?

57:00.459 --> 57:04.004
So you're telling me to get lost
now that you don't need me anymore?

57:04.087 --> 57:06.423
You've gone beyond proving
that you loved Dad.

57:08.342 --> 57:11.637
I'm not even your blood.
You can stop carrying this burden now.

57:11.720 --> 57:13.180
You mean brat.

57:16.266 --> 57:17.768
How could you say that to me?

57:18.435 --> 57:21.939
"What are we?"
Are you seriously asking me that?

57:22.689 --> 57:23.649
You brat.

57:24.232 --> 57:26.151
[voice trembling] You mean brat.

57:26.234 --> 57:29.029
What do you know? Do you know how I feel?

57:29.112 --> 57:31.531
You can't say those things
when you don't even know how I feel!

57:31.615 --> 57:33.158
I know you resent me too!

57:33.742 --> 57:35.786
[sorrowful music playing]

57:35.869 --> 57:38.705
I know you secretly resent me
for being the reason Dad died.

57:38.789 --> 57:42.501
And you've had to raise this mean brat
as your own for Dad's sake.

57:43.877 --> 57:45.921
[voice trembling] You can't even admit

57:46.004 --> 57:49.007
that you've resented me all this time
even though you do.

57:50.592 --> 57:51.677
You're right.

57:52.511 --> 57:53.762
I did resent you.

57:55.472 --> 57:59.393
You, for being stubborn,
and your dad, for leaving us like he did.

57:59.476 --> 58:02.562
I resented the guy who got drunk
and died before he was even punished.

58:02.646 --> 58:04.356
You think that's all?

58:04.439 --> 58:07.275
I even resented your mom
for dying that day of all days.

58:07.359 --> 58:09.861
I also resented myself
for letting you two go that day.

58:09.945 --> 58:12.155
I resented everything in the world.

58:12.239 --> 58:14.157
I didn't even want to go on living.

58:15.200 --> 58:17.536
[sighs shakily, sobs]

58:19.496 --> 58:20.497
But…

58:21.164 --> 58:23.250
you saved me that day.

58:26.628 --> 58:28.714
[melancholic music continues]

58:31.675 --> 58:32.926
[Bun-hong sighs]

58:43.061 --> 58:44.271
[Ho-su muffled] Mom.

58:46.898 --> 58:49.568
Oh! Ho-su!

58:49.651 --> 58:50.819
Mom.

58:50.902 --> 58:53.739
[sobbing] My gosh. Ho-su.

58:56.867 --> 58:58.952
[continues sobbing]

59:00.704 --> 59:01.830
Ho-su.

59:03.415 --> 59:05.375
You were on the brink of death,

59:06.710 --> 59:07.961
but you opened your eyes.

59:10.714 --> 59:13.467
And you called me "Mom."

59:13.550 --> 59:15.260
[breathes shakily]

59:15.927 --> 59:18.638
That's why you've been stuck
with me all this time.

59:19.723 --> 59:21.058
No, you held on to me.

59:22.059 --> 59:25.103
You held on to me
and made sure I didn't wash away.

59:25.979 --> 59:27.606
I'm alive

59:28.565 --> 59:30.609
because you held on to me.

59:33.028 --> 59:37.365
Your dad brought us together
so that we could hold on to each other.

59:40.869 --> 59:41.912
Ho-su.

59:42.662 --> 59:44.915
My love for your dad is a memory,

59:45.832 --> 59:48.835
but my love for you is my reason to live.

59:49.795 --> 59:52.923
You're the one keeping me alive.
If that's not family, then what is?

59:53.006 --> 59:54.049
What are we?

59:55.133 --> 59:58.678
You're my son, and I'm your mom.

01:00:01.098 --> 01:00:04.226
If you let go of my hand,
then how am I supposed to go on?

01:00:05.060 --> 01:00:07.687
So Ho-su, don't let go.

01:00:08.313 --> 01:00:11.274
Hold on to everything you can, okay?

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:16.571
[Ho-su sobs]

01:00:26.206 --> 01:00:28.291
[Ho-su continues sobbing]

01:00:29.417 --> 01:00:31.169
[music fades]

01:00:32.462 --> 01:00:34.005
- Mom, how's Grandma?
- Gosh.

01:00:34.548 --> 01:00:36.842
- She just fell asleep.
- What?

01:00:36.925 --> 01:00:38.593
- What is this? Give it to me.
- No, no.

01:00:38.677 --> 01:00:41.221
Give it to me.
Let's sit for a bit and then go.

01:00:41.304 --> 01:00:43.723
Gosh, what's all this?

01:00:43.807 --> 01:00:46.685
Why didn't you let us know
that Grandma's not doing well?

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:50.522
Why would I tell you two
when it's not even good news?

01:00:50.605 --> 01:00:51.731
She's okay now.

01:00:52.357 --> 01:00:55.193
It's a weekday. Why'd you come here?

01:00:55.694 --> 01:00:56.903
What about work?

01:00:58.655 --> 01:00:59.739
Ah…

01:01:00.991 --> 01:01:02.534
About that…

01:01:02.617 --> 01:01:04.911
What? Did something happen?

01:01:06.872 --> 01:01:08.081
Today…

01:01:09.958 --> 01:01:11.418
I quit my job.

01:01:12.169 --> 01:01:13.253
What?

01:01:15.005 --> 01:01:16.089
[exhales]

01:01:17.549 --> 01:01:21.303
Is it because of what happened
when you and Mi-ji switched?

01:01:21.386 --> 01:01:23.138
No, it's not because of that.

01:01:24.055 --> 01:01:25.640
Then what is it?

01:01:25.724 --> 01:01:28.476
Why did you suddenly quit
when you were doing so well?

01:01:28.560 --> 01:01:29.811
The thing is…

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:34.191
I wasn't doing so well.

01:01:35.066 --> 01:01:36.568
I was struggling a little.

01:01:38.486 --> 01:01:40.739
That's why Mi-ji switched places with me.

01:01:43.283 --> 01:01:44.910
I'm glad you quit, then.

01:01:46.328 --> 01:01:48.079
There are plenty of other companies.

01:01:49.331 --> 01:01:50.665
I'm sorry.

01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:53.043
For what?

01:01:53.877 --> 01:01:56.129
I feel like I keep disappointing you.

01:01:57.547 --> 01:01:59.841
You believed in me and supported me.

01:02:00.425 --> 01:02:02.093
I gave up on the exam too.

01:02:03.511 --> 01:02:06.097
I haven't seen anything
through to the end.

01:02:07.766 --> 01:02:09.142
[gentle music playing]

01:02:09.226 --> 01:02:11.144
[breathes deeply]

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:14.731
I stayed by your grandma's side all night,

01:02:16.942 --> 01:02:18.485
but the only thing I could do

01:02:19.569 --> 01:02:22.072
was hold her hand and pray.

01:02:23.698 --> 01:02:24.950
That reminded me of the past.

01:02:25.825 --> 01:02:27.702
When you were hospitalized as a baby,

01:02:28.411 --> 01:02:32.249
you were so young, but you were hooked up
to so many needles and machines.

01:02:33.166 --> 01:02:36.670
I prayed,
"Please just let her live one more day."

01:02:36.753 --> 01:02:38.838
The next time you were hospitalized,

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:42.592
I prayed,
"Please just get better this time."

01:02:45.178 --> 01:02:47.931
Those prayers kept getting answered,

01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:51.142
so I guess I got greedy.

01:02:52.852 --> 01:02:55.897
[breathes deeply] You're exactly…

01:02:58.108 --> 01:03:00.360
what I prayed you would be,

01:03:01.152 --> 01:03:03.071
so don't say that you disappointed me.

01:03:04.864 --> 01:03:06.658
Just do whatever you want to do.

01:03:17.627 --> 01:03:18.753
[sighs]

01:03:19.337 --> 01:03:20.880
[gentle music continues]

01:03:20.964 --> 01:03:21.923
[mutters]

01:03:24.551 --> 01:03:25.552
CLOTHES

01:03:31.182 --> 01:03:32.183
Gosh.

01:03:45.572 --> 01:03:47.240
INVESTMENT WORLD'S RISING STAR
HAN SE-JIN

01:03:47.324 --> 01:03:49.159
You're not tired of looking at that?

01:03:52.787 --> 01:03:54.039
[objects shuffling]

01:03:54.122 --> 01:03:55.874
[music fades]

01:03:56.499 --> 01:03:58.543
Are you packing up that house too?

01:03:59.878 --> 01:04:02.464
I'm just organizing
my grandfather's things for now.

01:04:02.547 --> 01:04:05.091
If I find a replacement,
then they may want to live there.

01:04:05.175 --> 01:04:07.052
Did you decide on a replacement?

01:04:07.761 --> 01:04:11.222
It seems like no one is up for
the challenge of farming new varieties.

01:04:13.641 --> 01:04:16.686
More importantly, you're here now.

01:04:17.312 --> 01:04:18.813
So that means you quit.

01:04:18.897 --> 01:04:20.273
And if you quit,

01:04:21.066 --> 01:04:24.778
that must mean you're ready
to respond to my offer.

01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:26.196
Am I right?

01:04:26.279 --> 01:04:30.408
To be honest, your offer
was a dream come true for me.

01:04:31.993 --> 01:04:34.621
You even offered me
a place to stay in the States.

01:04:35.372 --> 01:04:37.040
Honestly, the offer is more than generous.

01:04:37.123 --> 01:04:40.043
[laughs] Gosh,
it's not more than generous.

01:04:40.126 --> 01:04:42.837
You'll just be an intern.
The rest is up to how you do.

01:04:43.421 --> 01:04:44.714
Okay, let's cut to the chase.

01:04:44.798 --> 01:04:47.759
What have you decided to do, Mi-rae?

01:04:49.511 --> 01:04:52.097
[breathes deeply]

01:04:54.057 --> 01:04:55.141
I decline.

01:04:56.017 --> 01:04:58.770
Why? No, I won't accept that.

01:04:59.437 --> 01:05:01.356
You should come with me.

01:05:01.439 --> 01:05:03.858
Is it because it's an internship?
But it's your dream.

01:05:03.942 --> 01:05:05.652
This is a really great offer.

01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:08.738
I know. That's why I'm declining.

01:05:08.822 --> 01:05:10.490
I don't think I'm ready yet.

01:05:10.573 --> 01:05:12.534
You don't need any preparation.

01:05:13.243 --> 01:05:15.412
I'm not hiring you for personal reasons.

01:05:15.495 --> 01:05:17.455
I've watched you here all this time.

01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:20.458
I made that offer because I have faith
that you'd do really well.

01:05:20.542 --> 01:05:22.919
It's because I'm still not sure
about myself.

01:05:23.002 --> 01:05:25.422
If I go feeling like this, then,
no matter what I accomplish,

01:05:25.505 --> 01:05:27.924
I'll think that it's all thanks
to you, Se-jin.

01:05:28.007 --> 01:05:30.718
You're such a straight arrow.

01:05:30.802 --> 01:05:32.804
You really are just like my grandfather.

01:05:33.430 --> 01:05:34.931
[clicks tongue, inhales]

01:05:35.598 --> 01:05:37.392
So what are you going to do now?

01:05:38.017 --> 01:05:40.437
I want to see things through
to the very end here.

01:05:41.729 --> 01:05:43.273
See what through?

01:05:43.356 --> 01:05:45.066
Please let me take care of the farm.

01:05:45.150 --> 01:05:46.734
I'll be your replacement.

01:05:47.610 --> 01:05:48.987
[gentle music playing]

01:05:49.070 --> 01:05:51.531
You're choosing strawberries
over my offer?

01:05:52.157 --> 01:05:54.075
When I take a test,

01:05:54.159 --> 01:05:56.202
there's nothing worse than picking

01:05:56.286 --> 01:05:59.038
what seems like the right answer
over what I actually felt was right

01:05:59.122 --> 01:06:01.249
and then getting the question wrong.

01:06:01.332 --> 01:06:04.669
It makes me think that I got it wrong
because I didn't trust myself.

01:06:04.752 --> 01:06:05.628
[breathes deeply]

01:06:05.712 --> 01:06:08.173
I think the right answer
is to go to the States,

01:06:08.256 --> 01:06:11.468
but for some strange reason,
staying here feels more right to me.

01:06:15.430 --> 01:06:17.849
Will you be okay? Aren't you scared?

01:06:17.932 --> 01:06:19.642
Of course I am.

01:06:19.726 --> 01:06:23.313
But for once in my life,
I want to do what my heart tells me to do.

01:06:24.314 --> 01:06:25.607
Even if it's wrong.

01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:30.403
[groans]

01:06:30.487 --> 01:06:32.947
Let's go, so I can hand things over.

01:06:34.407 --> 01:06:35.450
[groans]

01:06:36.576 --> 01:06:38.286
[music fades]

01:06:38.369 --> 01:06:40.288
PROPOSED SIGN DESIGN
ROSA RESTAURANT

01:06:40.371 --> 01:06:42.859
Oh, is this what it would look like?

01:06:43.374 --> 01:06:46.586
What do you mean?
It looks just like what I drew.

01:06:47.086 --> 01:06:47.962
My gosh!

01:06:48.046 --> 01:06:50.798
[Mi-ji] Anyway, they said the sign
will take a few days.

01:06:50.882 --> 01:06:53.843
Let me go through the mail
in the meantime.

01:06:54.469 --> 01:06:56.095
That's just an ad.

01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:02.227
This is a notice about hygiene training.

01:07:02.852 --> 01:07:05.939
It says you can do it online,

01:07:06.022 --> 01:07:08.525
so I'll explain this later.

01:07:10.902 --> 01:07:13.446
Oh! This is from the court.

01:07:13.530 --> 01:07:14.489
What?

01:07:26.584 --> 01:07:28.795
SEOUL CENTRAL DISTRICT FAMILY COURT

01:07:28.878 --> 01:07:31.756
[soft melancholic music playing]

01:07:31.839 --> 01:07:34.759
APPLICANT'S REPRESENTATIVE
ATTORNEY LEE HO-SU

01:07:37.303 --> 01:07:38.263
Ah…

01:07:38.346 --> 01:07:40.473
It's a court decision letter.

01:07:41.015 --> 01:07:44.060
The correction request we… [clears throat]

01:07:45.019 --> 01:07:47.397
[voice trembling]
The correction request for the registry…

01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:50.233
It's the request… we made last time.

01:07:51.442 --> 01:07:53.361
It's been approved.

01:07:53.444 --> 01:07:54.654
Are you okay?

01:07:55.280 --> 01:07:57.407
Why are you suddenly emotional?

01:07:57.490 --> 01:07:58.575
[clears throat]

01:07:58.658 --> 01:08:01.286
It's just that,
all of a sudden, my throat…

01:08:01.953 --> 01:08:05.456
Is there some bad news written there?

01:08:06.916 --> 01:08:07.959
No.

01:08:08.876 --> 01:08:10.420
[chuckles] It's just that…

01:08:10.503 --> 01:08:13.756
seeing Ho-su's name here made me a little…

01:08:13.840 --> 01:08:16.301
Gosh, what's wrong with me?
I'm so sorry.

01:08:17.552 --> 01:08:18.886
Did you two break up?

01:08:18.970 --> 01:08:20.638
[music fades]

01:08:20.722 --> 01:08:25.476
What? How did you even know
we were dating when we never told you?

01:08:26.060 --> 01:08:30.607
Gosh, you really are sharper
than you look, Ms. Sang-wol.

01:08:31.357 --> 01:08:33.151
Why did he break up with you?

01:08:33.651 --> 01:08:35.111
[Mi-ji] It just happened.

01:08:35.820 --> 01:08:39.032
He's busy right now,
and I also have a lot to do.

01:08:41.075 --> 01:08:44.537
Talk to Ho-su again.

01:08:44.621 --> 01:08:47.290
It's not my place to tell you,

01:08:47.832 --> 01:08:49.917
but he has a bit of a situation.

01:08:51.586 --> 01:08:53.212
He's trying…

01:08:53.921 --> 01:08:56.883
not to burden you…

01:08:56.966 --> 01:08:58.301
I know, ma'am.

01:09:00.219 --> 01:09:01.679
I know everything.

01:09:02.305 --> 01:09:03.431
You do?

01:09:04.349 --> 01:09:06.976
You know everything,
but you still broke up with him?

01:09:07.477 --> 01:09:08.394
Yes.

01:09:08.478 --> 01:09:09.395
[Sang-wol] Why?

01:09:09.479 --> 01:09:11.397
It seems like you still like him.

01:09:12.065 --> 01:09:13.775
Even when I threw salt at you,

01:09:13.858 --> 01:09:16.486
you kept knocking on my door
until I opened it.

01:09:16.569 --> 01:09:19.697
Given your personality, I thought
you'd be protesting outside his apartment.

01:09:19.781 --> 01:09:20.698
Why aren't you?

01:09:21.991 --> 01:09:23.826
Because I know how he feels.

01:09:25.036 --> 01:09:26.788
I was like that too.

01:09:28.247 --> 01:09:30.500
I was so miserable being me…

01:09:32.502 --> 01:09:35.880
that I couldn't even step
outside of my room for a few years.

01:09:37.382 --> 01:09:38.424
Well…

01:09:38.508 --> 01:09:41.302
Then you should know better
since you overcame that yourself.

01:09:42.553 --> 01:09:44.263
I never did…

01:09:45.473 --> 01:09:46.933
overcome it.

01:09:48.226 --> 01:09:51.187
I only left my room
because my grandma collapsed.

01:09:51.771 --> 01:09:53.648
It's not like I made it out on my own.

01:09:53.731 --> 01:09:56.401
You made it out, so you overcame it.

01:09:57.527 --> 01:09:59.362
I may be here physically,

01:10:00.238 --> 01:10:01.489
but I'm still holed up.

01:10:03.491 --> 01:10:04.659
You know…

01:10:05.660 --> 01:10:08.996
I still can't close my bedroom door
when I'm alone.

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:12.291
I'm afraid that I won't be able
to make it out like I did before.

01:10:13.376 --> 01:10:14.377
[chuckles]

01:10:14.460 --> 01:10:17.630
It's ridiculous, right?
Why can't I just close the door?

01:10:18.798 --> 01:10:20.508
I don't know why I'm so scared.

01:10:21.509 --> 01:10:24.137
[sighs] After all of that drama,

01:10:24.762 --> 01:10:27.598
you'd think that I would've gotten
become a little stronger.

01:10:27.682 --> 01:10:29.100
But I couldn't even do that.

01:10:31.394 --> 01:10:34.731
I felt so pathetic and stupid
for being like that…

01:10:35.857 --> 01:10:38.901
so I pretended I was okay,
afraid someone might see through it.

01:10:40.820 --> 01:10:45.825
What can I possibly say to Ho-su
when I'm like this?

01:10:48.119 --> 01:10:49.620
What can I…

01:10:50.788 --> 01:10:52.165
possibly do for Ho-su…

01:10:53.374 --> 01:10:55.084
when I'm like this?

01:10:57.378 --> 01:10:59.422
[tender music playing]

01:11:01.674 --> 01:11:06.637
Can you only be there for him
if you can do something major?

01:11:09.265 --> 01:11:11.684
Can't you just stay by his side

01:11:11.768 --> 01:11:14.353
and do what you can for him?

01:11:15.938 --> 01:11:17.064
Mi-ji.

01:11:18.232 --> 01:11:19.650
Do what you're good at.

01:11:20.276 --> 01:11:21.277
[knocking on table]

01:11:21.819 --> 01:11:23.488
Knocking on people's hearts.

01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:26.240
- [knocking on table]
- [Sang-wol] "I'm here."

01:11:26.324 --> 01:11:29.368
"If you open the door,
I'll be right outside."

01:11:29.911 --> 01:11:33.456
You can keep knocking
and telling him that.

01:11:39.420 --> 01:11:41.422
Do you remember what you told me before?

01:11:42.256 --> 01:11:45.593
You held onto my hands like this,

01:11:47.470 --> 01:11:49.889
and you said that
you never know what might happen.

01:11:50.807 --> 01:11:53.434
You didn't know anything back then either.

01:11:54.769 --> 01:11:56.646
You didn't know the answer,

01:11:57.772 --> 01:11:59.649
but you still stayed by my side.

01:12:01.317 --> 01:12:04.403
[music swells]

01:12:16.582 --> 01:12:18.543
[music fades]

01:12:18.626 --> 01:12:21.087
SEOUL
DUSON

01:12:21.170 --> 01:12:22.964
CT SCAN APPOINTMENT SLIP
EEG APPOINTMENT SLIP

01:12:23.047 --> 01:12:24.674
[Bun-hong] Next time,

01:12:25.174 --> 01:12:26.926
when you go for your CT and your EEG,

01:12:27.552 --> 01:12:30.972
tell them,
"I did the hearing test last time."

01:12:32.515 --> 01:12:35.893
Don't forget your appointment date.
They'll text you the day before.

01:12:36.477 --> 01:12:39.480
If I'm not busy, I'll come to Seoul too.

01:12:42.608 --> 01:12:43.651
Why are you smiling?

01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:45.945
It just feels like before.

01:12:47.113 --> 01:12:49.740
I thought I was done causing you trouble…
[chuckles]

01:12:49.824 --> 01:12:51.409
…but I'm back to square one.

01:12:53.077 --> 01:12:54.662
That's ridiculous.

01:12:54.745 --> 01:12:56.289
You can't compare back then to now.

01:12:57.081 --> 01:12:59.166
Do you know how much paperwork
I go through every day?

01:12:59.250 --> 01:13:01.252
This is no trouble at all.

01:13:03.504 --> 01:13:04.589
[sighs]

01:13:07.341 --> 01:13:09.552
Why did you go through that alone?

01:13:09.635 --> 01:13:12.221
Were you that scared
that you'd never hear again?

01:13:14.891 --> 01:13:16.058
If I'm alone,

01:13:17.018 --> 01:13:19.145
I would just be scared,
and that would be it.

01:13:20.187 --> 01:13:21.856
But if I have someone by my side,

01:13:23.566 --> 01:13:25.568
I feel like I'd make them miserable too.

01:13:26.736 --> 01:13:27.737
[Ho-su chuckles softly]

01:13:27.820 --> 01:13:28.946
[sighs]

01:13:31.657 --> 01:13:33.159
You're just like your dad.

01:13:34.702 --> 01:13:37.580
Like father, like son.
You speak just like him.

01:13:39.540 --> 01:13:40.833
My dad?

01:13:45.171 --> 01:13:46.839
Before we got married,

01:13:47.757 --> 01:13:50.885
your dad broke up with me once.

01:13:53.262 --> 01:13:56.891
He kept saying
that he was making me miserable.

01:13:58.726 --> 01:14:01.646
He said that if I stayed with him,
I'd end up losing.

01:14:02.355 --> 01:14:05.566
He said that with the exact expression
you're making right now.

01:14:06.067 --> 01:14:08.444
I got so angry that I told him…

01:14:10.696 --> 01:14:14.742
that people can't win all the time.

01:14:15.993 --> 01:14:19.872
I said, "Someday, there will be a day
when you will have to lose for me too."

01:14:19.956 --> 01:14:22.375
[tender music playing]

01:14:22.458 --> 01:14:23.626
[Ho-su's father] Ho-su.

01:14:23.709 --> 01:14:26.796
Someday, you're going
to make someone miserable too.

01:14:26.879 --> 01:14:29.632
There will definitely be a moment

01:14:30.466 --> 01:14:32.843
when you force the person
by your side to lose.

01:14:32.927 --> 01:14:34.345
But you know, Ho-su…

01:14:35.179 --> 01:14:37.098
- Love isn't about…
- [Bun-hong] "Love isn't about…"

01:14:37.181 --> 01:14:40.017
[both overlapping]
…winning or losing. It's about…

01:14:40.518 --> 01:14:41.978
"…remaining on the same team

01:14:42.895 --> 01:14:45.439
until the very end even if you lose."

01:14:46.857 --> 01:14:48.567
Love is about staying together…

01:14:50.361 --> 01:14:52.697
even if you lose a hundred
or a thousand times.

01:14:56.867 --> 01:14:58.160
[Ho-su's father] Ho-su.

01:14:58.869 --> 01:14:59.954
Love isn't about…

01:15:00.037 --> 01:15:01.122
Hi.

01:15:01.747 --> 01:15:03.332
…winning or losing.

01:15:04.625 --> 01:15:07.503
It's about remaining on the same team
until the very end even if you lose.

01:15:07.586 --> 01:15:09.088
We should still do everything we can--

01:15:09.171 --> 01:15:12.341
You don't have to pretend
we're family when nobody is around.

01:15:13.426 --> 01:15:15.886
[Ho-su's father]
Love is about staying together

01:15:17.346 --> 01:15:20.057
even if you lose a hundred
or a thousand times.

01:15:21.434 --> 01:15:23.477
[tender music continues]

01:15:30.818 --> 01:15:31.902
[sniffles]

01:15:39.744 --> 01:15:41.746
[tender music continues]

01:15:42.455 --> 01:15:43.581
[Mi-ji] I…

01:15:44.665 --> 01:15:48.169
I still can't close my bedroom door
when I'm alone.

01:15:49.670 --> 01:15:52.965
I'm afraid that I won't be able
to make it out like I did before.

01:15:53.049 --> 01:15:54.216
[music fades]

01:15:54.300 --> 01:15:56.052
What can I…

01:15:57.136 --> 01:15:58.429
possibly do for Ho-su…

01:15:59.555 --> 01:16:01.390
when I'm like this?

01:16:08.481 --> 01:16:10.983
[Sang-wol] Can't you just stay by his side

01:16:11.067 --> 01:16:13.277
and do what you can for him?

01:16:14.779 --> 01:16:19.492
Do what you're good at.
Knocking on people's hearts.

01:16:22.495 --> 01:16:24.246
[soft music playing]

01:16:25.081 --> 01:16:26.373
[Sang-wol] "I'm here."

01:16:26.999 --> 01:16:30.086
"If you open the door,
I'll be right outside."

01:16:30.669 --> 01:16:33.923
You can keep knocking
and telling him that.

01:16:34.006 --> 01:16:36.217
[music turns uplifting]

01:16:42.139 --> 01:16:44.600
[Sang-wol] Do you remember
what you told me before?

01:16:45.684 --> 01:16:48.020
You said that you never know
what might happen.

01:16:48.813 --> 01:16:50.815
You didn't know the answer,

01:16:52.525 --> 01:16:54.735
but you still stayed by my side.

01:16:55.778 --> 01:16:58.030
[uplifting music continues]

01:17:07.414 --> 01:17:09.959
[Mi-ji] I'm going to make it out
for real this time.

01:17:13.546 --> 01:17:15.047
Everyone…

01:17:16.757 --> 01:17:18.259
is waiting outside.

01:17:19.218 --> 01:17:20.970
[uplifting music continues]

01:17:36.652 --> 01:17:38.445
[music turns tender]

01:17:40.281 --> 01:17:43.367
If you open the door,
I'll be right outside.

01:17:47.872 --> 01:17:49.206
So you can just…

01:17:50.583 --> 01:17:52.001
open the door at any time.

01:17:52.793 --> 01:17:55.462
[music swells]

01:18:12.688 --> 01:18:13.564
[knocking on door]

01:18:14.607 --> 01:18:15.900
Mi-ji.

01:18:15.983 --> 01:18:18.485
Open the door. Mi-ji!

01:18:19.195 --> 01:18:21.405
Mi-ji, Grandma's coming in.

01:18:22.031 --> 01:18:23.449
It's okay, my dear.

01:18:23.532 --> 01:18:25.910
Let's brush it off and get back up.

01:18:25.993 --> 01:18:27.745
[music calms]

01:18:27.828 --> 01:18:29.663
[Mi-ji sobbing]

01:18:43.093 --> 01:18:45.512
[uplifting music continues]

01:18:48.224 --> 01:18:50.517
[music swells]

01:19:10.037 --> 01:19:11.455
[Mi-ji breathing heavily]

01:19:11.538 --> 01:19:13.832
I just need to open the door.

01:19:14.333 --> 01:19:15.626
Just open the door…

01:19:17.878 --> 01:19:19.004
[door lock chimes]

01:19:19.088 --> 01:19:20.965
- [Mi-ji gasps] Ho-su!
- [music concludes]

01:19:21.048 --> 01:19:23.509
What are you doing here?

01:19:23.592 --> 01:19:26.470
I was just about to come to you…

01:19:28.013 --> 01:19:30.432
I'm sorry, Mi-ji.

01:19:31.892 --> 01:19:33.227
Uh…

01:19:33.310 --> 01:19:35.980
I was an idiot.
I shouldn't have done that to you.

01:19:36.063 --> 01:19:37.606
[Mi-ji] No.

01:19:37.690 --> 01:19:41.151
I wanted to go to you earlier, but…

01:19:42.111 --> 01:19:43.195
[Mi-ji whimpers]

01:19:43.779 --> 01:19:45.739
Please stay by my side, Mi-ji.

01:19:47.074 --> 01:19:49.368
[tender music playing]

01:19:50.244 --> 01:19:51.328
[sobs shakily]

01:19:52.246 --> 01:19:53.872
Please stay with me.

01:19:58.919 --> 01:20:00.838
[music swells]

01:20:13.892 --> 01:20:15.769
[Ho-su] The promise of a tomorrow

01:20:16.645 --> 01:20:19.064
is not born from hope, but from resolve.

01:20:19.148 --> 01:20:20.733
[tender music continues]

01:20:45.341 --> 01:20:47.551
Looking back,
the path I've walked is full of regrets.

01:20:47.634 --> 01:20:48.802
[music calms]

01:20:49.303 --> 01:20:51.638
[Ho-su]
And the road ahead is veiled in fear.

01:20:52.931 --> 01:20:55.309
Ms. Yu left the company today.

01:20:55.851 --> 01:20:57.853
She asked me to give this to you.

01:21:10.282 --> 01:21:11.825
[tender music continues]

01:21:15.371 --> 01:21:19.583
[Mi-rae] Even when you weren't by my side,
you were always with me in spirit.

01:21:20.667 --> 01:21:23.045
So please be gentle
and forgiving with yourself.

01:21:24.004 --> 01:21:25.464
Be kind to yourself

01:21:26.465 --> 01:21:27.674
as you were to me.

01:21:29.176 --> 01:21:30.844
[music fades]

01:21:30.928 --> 01:21:32.012
[door unlocks]

01:21:40.854 --> 01:21:42.064
[doorknob rattles]

01:21:49.446 --> 01:21:51.031
[theme song playing]

01:21:51.115 --> 01:21:52.199
[chuckles softly]

01:21:57.037 --> 01:21:59.123
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night… ♪

01:21:59.248 --> 01:22:02.167
[Ho-su in Korean] We found the resolve
to walk this uncertain path together.

01:22:02.251 --> 01:22:04.002
without knowing what lies ahead.

01:22:06.588 --> 01:22:08.966
Even if all that awaits us
is a pitiful ending,

01:22:10.259 --> 01:22:11.844
we will walk this path together

01:22:12.678 --> 01:22:14.054
until the very end.

01:22:14.138 --> 01:22:17.391
[in English]
♪ When you're feeling all alone ♪

01:22:19.309 --> 01:22:22.688
♪ When you're staying up all night ♪

01:22:24.022 --> 01:22:28.777
[singing in Korean]

01:22:29.862 --> 01:22:32.865
[singing in Korean continues]

01:22:32.948 --> 01:22:35.576
[in English] ♪ We're on the train ♪

01:22:35.659 --> 01:22:36.827
[singing in Korean]

01:22:36.910 --> 01:22:38.078
YU MI-JI

01:22:38.162 --> 01:22:40.205
[in Korean] If you use these,
it won't be organic.

01:22:40.289 --> 01:22:41.707
I'm not doing organic farming.

01:22:41.790 --> 01:22:45.377
[Se-jin] How about this? I invest
the initial capital and take eight.

01:22:45.461 --> 01:22:49.047
[Ok-hui] She's not interested in dating.

01:22:49.131 --> 01:22:50.799
What's going on between you two?

01:22:50.883 --> 01:22:52.593
Do you know Ho-su isn't well?

01:22:52.676 --> 01:22:55.345
[Ho-su] I want to try everything I can.
Meds, treatments, anything.

01:22:55.429 --> 01:22:58.265
Have you ever thought
about working with me?

01:22:58.348 --> 01:23:00.392
[Mi-ji] Hi, Mom.
What's wrong with Grandma?

01:23:00.476 --> 01:23:01.768
[Wol-sun softly] Mi-ji.

01:23:02.728 --> 01:23:03.812
[Mi-ji softly] Let's go.

01:23:04.813 --> 01:23:06.273
Let's go home, Grandma.

01:23:06.356 --> 01:23:09.318
- [song continues]
- [singing in Korean]

01:23:11.530 --> 01:23:13.530
Subtitle translation by Jane Jung
